  {
    "index": 9,
    "hash": "uV3IiKGU+7WDu1UTmzo1s74St28=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T15:34:47.255Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The `useNodeActions()` hook from `@powerhousedao/reactor-browser` returns an object with drive file/folder operations: `onAddFile(file: File, parent: Node | undefined)` adds a file under a parent folder; `onAddFolder(name, parent)` creates a folder; `onRenameNode(newName, node)` renames; `onCopyNode(src, target)` copies to a target folder; `onMoveNode(src, target)` moves; `onDuplicateNode(src)` duplicates in the current folder; `onAddAndSelectNewFolder(name)` creates and selects a new folder; `onRenameDriveNodes` renames drive nodes (defined `packages/reactor-browser/src/hooks/node-actions.ts:130`, returned at `:157`). That is **eight** functions, not seven. All return Promises. The drive structure uses `Node` (FileNode | FolderNode) hierarchy, queryable via `useNodesInSelectedDrive`, `useFileNodesInSelectedDrive`, `useFolderNodesInSelectedDrive`, and their folder-scoped variants.\n\n_Source-verified 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse source at v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T15:34:44.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T15:34:47.255Z"
    }
  },
